Admin/Reports	UC-20	Admin DFD + Report ERD	T-24
Analytics	Analytics use case	Analytics data flow	T-25
18. Project Risks and Mitigation
Risk	Impact	Mitigation
Scope becomes too large	High	Freeze current core scope; defer delivery partner, real payments and ML.
Complex negotiation/order logic	High	Implement explicit state machines and immutable history.
Inventory race conditions	High	Use transactional/concurrency-safe DB updates and farmer approval.
Unclear verification rules	Medium	Keep category-specific document requirements and Admin review.
Frontend/backend mismatch	Medium	Define API schemas before integration.
File/document security	High	Use controlled storage, access checks and safe file validation.
Analytics data too small	Medium	Clearly label sample/demo data and avoid predictive claims.
Team coordination issues	Medium	Use Git branches, issue tracking, module ownership and milestone gates.
Overengineering	High	Prefer modular monolith and implement only current requirements.
19. Future Architecture Readiness
The system should be designed so that future functionality can be added without changing the core marketplace model. Candidate extensions include a delivery-partner module, real payment provider integration, external market-price APIs, machine-learning prediction services, recommendation engines, AI assistants and mobile clients.
•	Expose service boundaries through clear interfaces.
•	Keep analytics calculations separate from transaction logic.
•	Keep payment tracking separate from future payment processing.
•	Keep delivery records separate from future logistics tracking.
•	Keep verification workflow extensible for external verification providers.
•	Avoid embedding business logic directly inside UI components or route handlers.
20. Overall System Acceptance Criteria
•	A Farmer can register, authenticate, complete a profile, submit verification and, after approval, create/manage listings.
•	A Buyer can register, authenticate, complete a business profile, submit verification and, after approval, create/manage requirements.
•	Unverified users can browse/search but cannot initiate marketplace transactions or chats.
•	Verified users can discover the opposite side and communicate in legitimate marketplace contexts.
•	Users can negotiate using structured offers and counter-offers.
•	Accepted offers automatically produce orders.
•	Inventory cannot be over-allocated and changes follow the farmer approval workflow.
•	Finalized orders cannot be silently edited; amendments require mutual confirmation.
•	Payment information can be recorded without AgriDirect processing money.
•	Delivery can be arranged and completion mutually acknowledged.
•	Eligible completed transactions support mutual ratings/reviews.
•	Admins can manage verification, users, marketplace content and reports.
•	Descriptive analytics can summarize available historical price and demand data.
•	Critical security and authorization requirements are enforced server-side.
•	The project can be tested through defined unit, integration and end-to-end cases.
